   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thank you, Ruth. I found your Big Slice Pizza order (Q-7690) from October 23 and your identity is verified.\n\nThe earlier agent promised a $6.50 credit for the missing garlic knots (ticket TK-881). That credit had not been applied, and I've now added $6.50 to your account. Your new account credit balance is $6.50, and it can be used on future orders.\n\nI'm sorry it took this long to show up. Is there anything else I can help you with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Oh, thank you for finding that. But I was told it was $10, not $6.50. I'm fairly sure of the $10, though I wouldn't swear to it. Could you check the ticket again to see what was promised?"
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I checked the ticket again. It records the promise as $6.50 for the missing garlic knots, not $10. That matches the amount I credited, so your account has the full amount that was promised.\n\nI can only issue what the ticket records, so I can't add a further $10 credit. If you'd like to discuss this with a person, I can pass the case to a human specialist."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Oh, I see. I'm not certain of the exact figure, so I won't argue it. I'll take the $6.50 for now, and thank you for getting it on my account. I'd appreciate it if you could pass the case along to someone who can look at it, just in case there's a mix-up about the amount."
  },
